<title>USA: U.S. NAPM index in 57.1 in May vs 54.2 in April.</title>
<headline>U.S. NAPM index in 57.1 in May vs 54.2 in April.</headline>
<dateline>TEMPE, Ariz. 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Association of Purchasing Management (NAPM) on Monday said its index of maufacturing activity rose to 57.1 in May from 54.2 in April.</p>
<p>A listing of the main NAPM components follows:</p>
<p>		    May  April  Mar  Feb  Jan  Dec  Nov  Oct  Sept</p>
<p>PMI		57.1  54.2  55.0  53.1 52.0 53.8 52.7 50.2 51.7</p>
<p>Production     57.0  56.6  56.8  59.5 58.1 58.5 58.6 56.6 54.1</p>
<p>New Orders     64.2  57.9  60.3  57.7 53.5 58.2 55.4 51.6 56.3</p>
<p>Supplier Del   55.2  53.4  53.6  51.3 48.5 51.6 51.5 50.7 49.7</p>
<p>Inventories    47.6  41.2  43.7  41.2 44.4 44.9 41.8 38.9 44.8</p>
<p>Employment     52.6  52.8  51.6  45.4 48.7 47.5 47.5 45.5 46.9</p>
<p>Prices	   48.4  49.6  50.9  55.1 51.4 50.8 45.9 47.1 51.2</p>
<p>Export Orders  54.3  55.7  57.3  52.1 54.6 56.3 55.8 56.1 56.8 Imports	  54.2  52.9  48.8  50.9 51.8 52.7 52.5 53.8 51.8</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
